\label{prop: exact two point function for WUSF on regular trees}
 	Let $\mathbb{P}$ denote the law of WUSF on the regular tree $\mathbb{T}_{b+1}$, where $b\geq2$. Let $x,y\in V(G)$ be two arbitrary vertices and $\{x\leftrightarrow y\}$
 	denote the event that $x,y$ are in the same tree of WUSF. Set $n=\textnormal{dist}(x,y)$ to be the graph distance of $x,y$. Then 
 	\begin{equation}\label{eq: two point function for WUSF on the toy model}
 	\mathbb{P}[x\leftrightarrow y]=\frac{1}{b^n}[1+n\cdot\frac{b-1}{b+1}].
 	\end{equation}
 	In particular, the probability that the tree $T_x$ intersects with a high slab $L_n(x)$ decays exponentially: 
 	\[
 	\mathbb{P}[T_x\cap L_n(x)\neq\emptyset]=\frac{1}{b^n}[1+n\cdot\frac{b-1}{b+1}]\asymp ne^{-t_0n},n\geq1.
 	\]

\begin{equation}\label{eq: two point function for WUSF on the toy model}
 	\mathbb{P}[x\leftrightarrow y]=\frac{1}{b^n}[1+n\cdot\frac{b-1}{b+1}].
 	\end{equation}

\[
